  "body": "## What changed\n\n- New undoable command `DuplicateTool` (`crates/app/src/commands/tool_duplicate.rs`). It copies a document tool as a new tool. The copy has the same definition (geometry, cutting data), holder body, stick-out, drawn cutter and component stack. It lands the same `ToolRecords` list that `DeleteTool` snapshots. Only the tool number is new (`ToolRecords::renumbered`).\n- The copy gets a free name: `<stem> (2)`, `(3)`, and so on. The stem drops a trailing ` (n)`, so the copy of `EM (2)` is `EM (3)`.\n- The copy gets the next free tool number from `tool_reservations::allocate`, the same rule as `AddTool`. The command refuses by name, before anything enters the history: an unknown name, an entity that is not a tool, no free tool number, no free name.\n- New MCP tool `duplicate_tool { name }` (`crates/app/src/mcp/tool_duplicate.rs`, one registration line). It returns `{ source, tool, number }`. The generated reference `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` and the MCP guide table have the new row.\n- UI: the tool editor footer in the tool library window enables **Duplicate**. A click queues `CommandKind::DuplicateTool`. The window then opens the copy in the editor. The copy is of the tool as it is applied, not of the unapplied draft (the same rule as Duplicate on a user holder, #4338).\n- Decision file: `docs/decisions/4340-duplicate-tool.md`.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nTool editor footer before (Duplicate disabled) and after (Duplicate enabled), then the window after a click on Duplicate (the copy is open):\n\n![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4482/before.png)\n![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4482/after.png)\n![after-copy-open](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4482/after-copy-open.png)\n\n## Tests\n\nPinning tests (all green on head `c3143334d`, log `gate-4340-c3143334d.log`):\n\n- `tool_library_holders`: `duplicate_tool::duplicate_copies_the_stack_and_the_body_in_one_undo_step`, `duplicate_tool::duplicate_keeps_a_library_holder`, `duplicate_tool::copy_names_count_up_from_the_stem`, `duplicate_tool::duplicate_refuses_an_unknown_name_and_a_non_tool`, `duplicate_tool::mcp_duplicate_tool_runs_the_command_and_undo_removes_it`.\n- `camcraft-ui` lib: `tool_library_frame::duplicate_opens_the_copy_and_is_one_undo_step` (new), `tool_library_frame::the_tool_editor_has_the_back_button_and_the_apply_footer` (Duplicate is now enabled).\n- `camcraft-app` lib: `commands::tool::duplicate::tests::the_stem_drops_only_a_numeric_counter`.\n\nGate results:\n\n- Final head `2d0bf9ef2` (a merge of `origin/main`; one hand-resolved hunk: the tool count line of the generated `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md`, now 139). Log `gate-4340-2d0bf9ef2.log`: `mcp_doc_drift` 9 passed, `tool_library_holders` 68 passed, `tool_library` 25 passed, `mcp_delete_tool` 3 passed, `camcraft-app` lib `duplicate` 1 passed, `camcraft-ui` lib `tool_library` 122 passed, clippy `-p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings` clean.\n\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`) on `c1a7615c1`: 393 steps, 392 ok, 1 failed. The failed step is `example_catalog` (`catalog_3d_rough_finish::rebuilds`, slow >60 s on the loaded builder). The test passes alone on `c3143334d` (7 passed, 55.9 s). This change does not touch a toolpath or a post.\n- `mcp_doc_drift`: 9 passed (the reference and the guide have `duplicate_tool`).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean on `c3143334d` (the first run found one unused import in the new test; fixed in `c3143334d`).\n- Light lane: not run. No toolpath, post or heavy test changed.\n- `crates/ui` `#[test]` count: 2019 at the merge base, 2020 at the head.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The refusal \"no free tool number\" needs 99,999 tools or a full machine table. No test makes it. The refusal is the `allocate` error of `AddTool`, with the source tool's name in front.\n- The copy of a lathe tool with a lathe body was not tested by itself. It uses the same record list.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #4339 (tool stacks) and #4389 (Holders page) are in work. This PR touches `commands/tool.rs` (3 lines at the end), `commands/tool_delete.rs` (one new method), `commands/mod.rs` (one re-export), `ui/src/state.rs` (one variant, one match arm) and the tool library footer. merge-impact output is in the hand-back.\n\nProcess change: no\nEffort: high\nChangelog: Tool library: Duplicate in the tool editor copies the tool with its holder and component stack, under a free name and tool number, as one undo step; MCP `duplicate_tool` does the same.\n\nFixes #4340\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
